<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Yique</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">293 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Yique was fought in 293 BCE near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-of-qin">State of Qin</a> and the allied armies of Han and Wei. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bai-qi">Bai Qi</a> won a crushing victory; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/records-of-the-grand-historian">Shiji</a> claims 240,000 enemy dead. The battle broke the power of Han and Wei to resist Qin and opened the way for its further expansion in the central plain.</p></div>
